# clause-runtime-zig — Design

Zig implementation of the clause runtime. Consumes the C ABI
(clause-runtime-abi); implements the entry points with a Clause-
IR interpreter, scratch-var folding, and generative expansion.

## Scope

- Arena allocator — per-session state owning compile-time
  buffers.
- IR interpreter — evaluates macro bodies + generative subgraph
  blueprints against the incoming ABI node buffers.
- Scratch-var evaluator — folds compile-time expressions to byte
  blobs the compiler re-inserts into the AST.
- TokenStream emitter — macros return AbiToken arrays.
- Error reporter — maps Zig-side failures to AbiDiagnostic.

## Non-scope

- The ABI contract itself (clause-runtime-abi).
- The compiler-side dispatch (clause-runtime-driver).
- Runtime performance tuning (post-Phase 6).

## Build integration

- `build.zig` drives the Zig compilation.
- Output: `zig-out/lib/libclause_runtime.{so|dylib|dll}`.
- Target-triple-specific builds; a distribution bundle pairs the
  Rust compiler binary with the matching dylib for each supported
  platform.

## Dependencies

- Standard Zig library only. No third-party Zig packages. No
  runtime allocator — arena-only.

